    <!-- The Cruciform knot: one band runs corner to corner around an empty square (the
         void), throwing a crossed loop out on each side. The strand leaving a corner always
         passes over, so the crossings alternate over/under along the band. The under strand
         is simply broken at each crossing, which is why the path has four open runs.
         Fits the 66dp adaptive-icon safe zone exactly (loop tips at r = 33). -->
